      "walkthrough": [
        "Integrate $f'(x) = 6x^{-1/2} - 4x^{-3/2}$ with respect to $x$:\n$$y = \\int \\left(6x^{-1/2} - 4x^{-3/2}\\right)\\,dx = \\frac{6x^{1/2}}{\\frac{1}{2}} - \\frac{4x^{-1/2}}{-\\frac{1}{2}} + c$$",
        "Simplify the integrated expression:\n$$y = 12x^{1/2} + 8x^{-1/2} + c$$",
        "Substitute the point $(4, 7)$ to solve for the constant of integration $c$:\n$$7 = 12(4)^{1/2} + 8(4)^{-1/2} + c = 12(2) + 8\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) + c = 24 + 4 + c = 28 + c \\implies c = -21$$",
